      "start_seconds": 1.12,
      "end_seconds": 6.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.14,
      "end_seconds": 12.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.05,
      "end_seconds": 19.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "I wanted to get pain spreading all over looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.81,
      "end_seconds": 22.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "tell me your medicines please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.61,
      "end_seconds": 28.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "I take diclofenac, when needed for the joint pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.57,
      "end_seconds": 32.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "right and what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.6,
      "end_seconds": 46.58,
      "duration_seconds": 11.98,
      "text": "It's 50 milligrams. I take escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety. Ibuprofen, 600 milligrams, three times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 48.65,
      "end_seconds": 53.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 300 milligrams"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.3,
      "end_seconds": 62.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.66,
      "end_seconds": 66.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "No I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.95,
      "end_seconds": 74.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.78,
      "text": "Okay give me more detail on it whatever comes to mind. Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.36,
      "end_seconds": 83.88,
      "duration_seconds": 8.52,
      "text": "Mm I'd call it moderate. It's all the time. Oh and a sudden severe tummy pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.03,
      "end_seconds": 87.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.66,
      "end_seconds": 94.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "it happens all the time. There was vomiting, yes, but that went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.23,
      "end_seconds": 112.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "and what about fever or diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.32,
      "end_seconds": 116.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "No, no fever or diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.06,
      "end_seconds": 120.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "How about blood in the vomit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.98,
      "end_seconds": 125.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "nope no blood in the vomit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.71,
      "end_seconds": 129.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.12,
      "end_seconds": 133.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "no, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.76,
      "end_seconds": 136.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.39,
      "end_seconds": 141.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.95,
      "end_seconds": 145.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.49,
      "end_seconds": 149.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.11,
      "end_seconds": 154.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Okay, do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.23,
      "end_seconds": 162.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "I have arthritis in my knees i, I have anxiety, for nearly five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.17,
      "end_seconds": 165.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Okay, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.71,
      "end_seconds": 168.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "no, not at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.9,
      "end_seconds": 190.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Right, before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.33,
      "end_seconds": 194.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "no, I've never reacted to to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 196.72,
      "end_seconds": 202.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "okay so the vitals from earlier pulse 126 blood pressure 135 over 73 respiratory rate 20."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.19,
      "end_seconds": 204.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Good thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.11,
      "end_seconds": 210.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a a second make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.11,
      "end_seconds": 212.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.26,
      "end_seconds": 217.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Right tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.39,
      "end_seconds": 234.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Your tummy is rigid like a board and very tender everywhere, and you are lying completely still."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.59,
      "end_seconds": 240.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "all finished, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.95,
      "end_seconds": 263.42,
      "duration_seconds": 10.47,
      "text": "From what you've told me and and what I found, I'd lean towards a perforated stomach ulcer. Another possibility is pancreatitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.15,
      "end_seconds": 269.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.37,
      "end_seconds": 284.56,
      "duration_seconds": 13.19,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like a perforated stomach ulcer, but I'd like to confirm i want an erect chest X-ray done, that's for possible perforation"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.21,
      "end_seconds": 288.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "how long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.79,
      "end_seconds": 315.72,
      "duration_seconds": 25.93,
      "text": "Let's book urgent blood tests to look into acute abdomen. Nothing to eat or drink, you need an operation urgently. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Book a review straight away. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.73,
      "end_seconds": 321.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "No, uh, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.13,
